PART A -- ADDITIONAL PERMISSION AND SCOPE

1. Internal business use

The licensor grants an additional permitted purpose under Part B: use,
installation, copying, and modification of the software for the internal
business operations of you and your company, including commercial engineering,
design, manufacturing, facility operation, and maintenance. This includes
employees and contractors acting on your company's behalf, and internal
deployment accessible only to those people.

You may charge for engineering, design, consulting, construction, and
maintenance work performed using the software. You may give resulting reports,
calculations, drawings, and project data to clients and use those outputs in
paid contracts. Outputs are not the software merely because the software
generated them; this exception does not cover software source or executable
code included in an output.

2. Software commercialization is not granted

Neither this additional permission nor the noncommercial purposes in Part B
grant permission to sell, resell, rent, or license access to the software or
its modified or derivative versions for a fee. They do not grant permission
to bundle it into a paid software, hardware, or subscription product, or to
provide its substantial functionality to external users as a paid hosted or
managed software service. A separate written license from the licensor is
required for those activities. Free noncommercial sharing, testing, and
modification remain available under Part B.

Optional human installation, training, or support services may be charged
separately, provided obtaining or using the software is not conditioned on
purchasing those services, and the charge is not a disguised software or
software-access fee. Merely calling a paid software product an engineering
service does not make it a permitted internal use.

3. Notices and other terms

Copies distributed with this additional permission must retain this entire
LICENSE file, including Part A, Part B, the Required Notices, and the associated
copyright notices. Except for the additional permitted purpose expressly
granted above, all terms of Part B apply. No endorsement or trademark license
is granted. The licensor may offer separate commercial licenses.

4. Historical and third-party rights

These current terms start with the commit that first introduces this LICENSE
file and apply to the edition released with it and subsequent editions unless
expressly replaced. They do not withdraw, restrict, or retroactively change
rights already granted in earlier MIT-licensed versions, including commit
f8e92eab6f9c03262378c87591e8600ec3910e17. The historical MIT text is preserved
in LICENSE_LEGACY_MIT. Its inclusion does not offer the new additions and
modifications in this edition under MIT.

Third-party components retain their own licenses, as described in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Part A is project-specific additional permission; this
combination must not be described as unmodified PolyForm Noncommercial, MIT,
or an OSI-approved open-source license.

